    {
      "title": "How It Works",
      "content": "The AGENT P OISON approach uses a constrained optimization scheme to optimize the backdoor trigger. The optimization objective is to maximize the retrieval of malicious demonstrations while maintaining the coherence of the triggered queries. The approach consists of four steps: initialization, gradient approximation, constraint filtering, and token replacement.",
